30,2,,status,Midori,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,1,talk,May,,"It turns out we've actually had some wins! The old contactless trial and late-evening pilots were successful, though some of the lane-priority work from the accessibility push didn't exactly stick. History is actually useful!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"My findings are a bit more sobering. Our late-turn pool is practically a ghost town, and we are leaning heavily on overtime just to keep the lights on and the tracks clear.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Midori,,"I've found something quite curious. While people complain about crowding, the platform counts are stable. The real issue is that passengers are losing most of their time waiting for connections, not in queues.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"It seems we have some challenges ahead. I found that work in the pre-war shells is quite risky due to hidden voids, and the ferry and rail offices are still struggling to agree on data terms.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"I have noticed a worrying trend in the ledger. Our technology and operating subsidies are being trimmed, while the fees we pay to ticketing contractors are now outweighing our resurfacing budget. We are committing to high recurring costs.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,May,,"@Jonathan, if the ticketing fees are eating the budget, maybe we should look at those old contactless wins I found? It might be time to stop paying the contractors and do it ourselves.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@May, a charming suggestion, but building our own system requires people to manage it. If the late-turn pool is already exhausted, I wonder who would handle the midnight updates.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Benjamin, that is a very good point. We must be careful not to add more pressure to the staff. But if the delays are actually in the connections, perhaps we can find a solution that doesn't require more manpower?","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Midori, that is a lovely way to look at it. I am just worried that if we choose a plan involving those old station shells, we might find surprises that stop everything for weeks.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shizue, I share your caution. Between the hidden voids in the shells and the rising paving rates I discovered, any heavy construction could quickly spiral into a financial burden we cannot sustain.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,May,,"@Shizue, if the shells are such a nightmare, we should probably steer clear of them. Let's stick to the things that actually worked before—like those pilots—rather than gambling on a hole in the ground!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@May, your enthusiasm for the past is refreshing. However, we must remember that a ""successful pilot"" often relies on a dedicated team that doesn't exist in the current roster. We cannot simply wish the staff into existence.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Benjamin, I understand your concern. Perhaps we can look for a plan that optimizes the existing flow of passengers to reduce those connection wait times without needing a massive new team to manage it?","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Benjamin, you are so right to care for the staff. We must be gentle with them. I also wonder if we should avoid any plans requiring the ferry and rail offices to agree, as they seem quite stuck.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shizue, I agree. If the operators cannot agree on data terms, any plan requiring their coordination will likely stall. We should seek a path that is fiscally sustainable and operationally simple.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,4,talk,May,,"@Jonathan, ""operationally simple"" is my favorite phrase! Let's find something that doesn't require a miracle from the staff or a handshake between feuding offices. I'm ready to see the candidates!","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,I concur. Let us hope the candidates offer us a solution that respects both our budget and the sanity of our remaining crews. I am quite ready.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,Midori,,I agree with everyone. I hope we find a plan that truly helps the passengers save time while keeping things harmonious for the staff and the budget. I am ready too!,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Shizue,,It has been such a pleasure hearing all your thoughts. I feel we have a very clear understanding of the risks now. I am ready to see the candidates as well.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,It is a comfort to see us in such agreement. Let us hope the options before us are as balanced and serene as our current consensus. I am ready.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
53,3,,status,Shizue,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
54,3,,status,May,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
55,3,,status,Midori,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
56,3,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
57,3,1,talk,May,,"I'm leaning toward A! It brings back the success of those contactless pilots I found, and it solves Jonathan's headache with those expensive ticketing contractors. It's a win-win!","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"I must disagree with May. Candidate A requires the ferry and rail offices to agree on data terms, which Shizue noted is currently a stalemate. It is a digital dream on a foundation of bureaucratic sand.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""May"",""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Midori,,"I agree with Benjamin. Candidate A seems too risky given the disagreement between operators. I'm more interested in B, as it could address the connection delays I found without needing the pre-war shells.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"I agree with Midori. Candidate B seems like a gentle solution. It avoids the hidden voids in the old shells that would plague Candidate C, and it doesn't require the feuding offices to agree.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"I must be cautious with Candidate B. The rebuilt boarding islands and dedicated lanes would involve significant paving, and as I noted, paving rates are climbing while our operating subsidies are being trimmed. It may be a costly commitment.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,May,,"@Jonathan, if B is too pricey, what about D? It's based on the late-evening pilot that actually hit its cost targets! It's a proven concept that doesn't require digging holes or fighting with contractors.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@May, I admire your optimism, but Candidate D is a fantasy. My research shows the late-turn pool is already exhausted; extending hours would be like asking a marathon runner to sprint another ten miles.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@Benjamin, you're right to worry about the staff. If the crews are already exhausted, Candidate D would be unfair to them. I still feel Candidate B is the most helpful for passengers who are losing time on connections.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Jonathan, I understand your worries about the costs. But perhaps a few boarding islands are a smaller risk than the weeks of delays we would face with the voids in Candidate C? It feels like the safest path for everyone.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shizue, you make a fair point. While paving is expensive, it is a predictable cost compared to the unknown depths of the pre-war shells. Candidate B seems the most stable choice if we avoid the deeper excavations.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,May,,"@Midori, @Shizue, you've almost won me over! If B is the only way to fix those connection delays without breaking the staff or the budget, I can get behind it. It's better than a gamble!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Midori"",""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems we have reached a most elegant consensus. Candidate B avoids the bureaucratic deadlock of A, the structural nightmares of C, and the operational impossibility of D. It is the only choice that doesn't treat our staff as an infinite resource.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Midori,,I am so glad we could find a path that respects everyone's concerns. Candidate B helps the passengers save time on their journeys while remaining mindful of our staff and the budget. I'm very happy with this!,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Shizue,,It warms my heart to see us all in such harmony. Candidate B is a thoughtful choice that protects our workers and avoids those hidden surprises in the ground. I am very happy to vote for it.,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I concur. While the paving costs are a concern, Candidate B is the most balanced option. It avoids the operational strain of D and the structural risks of C, providing a serene path forward. I vote for B.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,4,talk,May,,"I'm in! It's not as flashy as a digital revolution, but it's the smartest move we've got. I vote for B!","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,Logic dictates that B is the only viable path. It is the only option that doesn't assume our staff are magical beings capable of working without sleep. I vote for B.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,4,talk,Midori,,I am very happy that we have found a solution that balances the needs of the passengers with the well-being of our staff. I vote for B!,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Shizue,,I am so glad we have all found a way to agree. It is a wonderful feeling to move forward together. I happily cast my vote for Candidate B.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,I am in complete agreement. Candidate B is the most sustainable and peaceful choice for the network. I vote for B.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
